    ontoksd:hasInstructionalStatement "Analyze TSP and timetabling submissions and reasons for TLE in relation to input size, algorithmic strategy, resource limits and problem formulation."@en,
        "Explain computability/termination limits and distinguish them from practical time limits and NP-hardness."@en,
        "Preserve the source simulation/testing objective while documenting conditional C03 activation. Do not treat every timeout as an infinite loop."@en,
        "Provide an SBC-format article with hypotheses, characterization of TSP/PT, manager-facing answers, the FSM and illustrative examples."@en,
        "Represent observable Online Judge workflow and AC, WA, TLE, CE and RE outcomes with an FSM, explaining model and evaluation limits."@en,
        "State the formulation before assigning a complexity class: decision TSP and optimization TSP are different formulations; timetabling depends on its constraints."@en,
        "The experiment evaluating TSP/PT code at different input sizes is an extra challenge; no benchmark result or executed evaluation is asserted."@en ;
